"""Rebuild the reviewed final notebook without claiming unexecuted results."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
NOTEBOOK = json.loads("{\"cells\":[{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"id\":\"title\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"# NLP Final — AI-assisted lost and found matching\\n\",\"**ICS 3202 · Deliverable 3 | Strathmore University**\\n\",\"Alex Muriithi (177298) · Nimrod Kobia (168357) · Louis Muturi (191603)\\n\",\"\\n\",\"**Objective:** given a lost report, return a ranked list of possible found items and a plain-language explanation for office staff. The system assists a human decision; it does not establish ownership or authorize release.\\n\",\"\\n\",\"**One assessed notebook:** this file contains the development process from problem definition to data collection, preprocessing, modelling, evaluation and the operational demonstration. The historical supervised base model remains in [LogisticRegression_Baseline.ipynb](LogisticRegression_Baseline.ipynb). The active method is TF-IDF, not that classifier.\\n\",\"\\n\",\"**Run:** from this checkout, install requirements.txt and run all cells in a fresh Python kernel. No Firebase cloud credentials or hosted services are needed for the notebook. Code cells are intentionally cleared until genuinely executed. The final optional HTTP preview is not an application test.\\n\",\"\\n\",\"| Data mining stage | Notebook section |\\n\",\"|---|---|\\n\",\"| Business / problem understanding | Introduction |\\n\",\"| Data collection and understanding | 1 |\\n\",\"| Data preparation and validation | 2 |\\n\",\"| Modelling | 3–4 |\\n\",\"| Validation and evaluation | 5–6 |\\n\",\"| Operational evaluation and deployment | 7–8 |\\n\",\"| Interpretation, limitations and next steps | 9 |\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"id\":\"data-understanding\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"## 1. Data collection and understanding\\n\",\"Two separate sources serve different purposes. The office aggregate transcription records unclaimed-item quantities: 388 in June–July and 299 in August 2026. It contains no individual report descriptions or verified lost–found pairs, so it cannot train or test the matching model. One disposal destination is blank; retain it as unknown.\\n\",\"The second source consists of authored fictional item reports and no-match examples. It supplies controlled expected answers for development, not real campus accuracy. Independent review is pending.\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"id\":\"environment\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"import csv, json, sys, platform\\n\",\"from pathlib import Path\\n\",\"from tempfile import TemporaryDirectory\\n\",\"from collections import Counter, defaultdict\\n\",\"import numpy as np\\n\",\"import pandas as pd\\n\",\"import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\n\",\"import sklearn\\n\",\"from IPython.display import display\\n\",\"ROOT = next((p for p in (Path.cwd(), *Path.cwd().parents)\\n\",\"             if (p / \\\"scripts/prepare_ranking_benchmark.py\\\").is_file()), None)\\n\",\"if ROOT is None:\\n\",\"    raise FileNotFoundError(\\\"Open the notebook within SemProject_MLEngine\\\")\\n\",\"if str(ROOT) not in sys.path:\\n\",\"    sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\\n\",\"print(\\\"Python:\\\", platform.python_version(), \\\"| scikit-learn:\\\", sklearn.__version__)\\n\",\"print(\\\"Repository:\\\", ROOT.name)\"],\"execution_count\":null,\"outputs\":[]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"id\":\"office-profile\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"inventory_path = ROOT / 'data/raw/campus/office_inventory_aggregate.csv'\\n\",\"with inventory_path.open(encoding='utf-8', newline='') as stream:\\n\",\"    inventory = list(csv.DictReader(stream))\\n\",\"totals = defaultdict(int); category_totals = defaultdict(lambda: defaultdict(int))\\n\",\"for row in inventory:\\n\",\"    quantity = int(row['quantity'])\\n\",\"    totals[row['period']] += quantity\\n\",\"    category_totals[row['period']][row['category']] += quantity\\n\",\"print('period | rows | quantity | missing disposal destination')\\n\",\"for period in totals:\\n\",\"    rows = [row for row in inventory if row['period'] == period]\\n\",\"    missing_destination = sum(not row['dispose_to'].strip() for row in rows)\\n\",\"    print(f\\\"{period} | {len(rows)} | {totals[period]} | {missing_destination}\\\")\\n\",\"    print('  category totals:', dict(category_totals[period]))\\n\",\"print('Used for training or scoring: no. The table has no item-level match labels.')\"],\"execution_count\":null,\"outputs\":[]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"id\":\"office-chart\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"inventory_summary = pd.DataFrame(category_totals).T.fillna(0)\\n\",\"display(inventory_summary)\\n\",\"ax = inventory_summary.plot(kind='bar', figsize=(8, 3.5), rot=0)\\n\",\"ax.set(title='Office inventory quantities by category', xlabel='Reporting period', ylabel='Reported quantity')\\n\",\"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\"plt.show()\"],\"execution_count\":null,\"outputs\":[]},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"id\":\"preparation\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"## 2. Data preparation: construct labelled reports and split the data\\n\",\"The 24 controlled item groups each supply one found and one corresponding lost report. Within each split, pairing the eight lost reports with eight found reports produces 64 labelled pairs (8 positive, 56 negative); across three splits this yields 192 pairs (24 positive, 168 negative). Three additional no-match queries do not have a designated positive pair. The candidate inventory contains 24 found records.\\n\",\"\\n\",\"A label of 1 means the authored example defines the same item; 0 means a different item. Empty brand, colour or date values are unknown, not invented. Related item groups stay within one split to reduce leakage (information from testing entering development). Train develops parameters, validation chooses settings, test evaluates held-out queries. All three splits share a fixed retrieval inventory, but offline fitting uses training reports only.\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"id\":\"prepare-records\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"# Use the same fixture files and transformations as prepare_ranking_benchmark.py.\\n\",\"SOURCE = ROOT / \\\"data\\\" / \\\"fixtures\\\" / \\\"ranking\\\"\\n\",\"_NOTEBOOK_TMP = TemporaryDirectory(prefix=\\\"nlp-ranking-\\\")\\n\",\"RUN_DIR = Path(_NOTEBOOK_TMP.name)\\n\",\"DATA = RUN_DIR / \\\"ranking\\\"\\n\",\"output_dir = DATA\\n\",\"def read(name):\\n\",\"    with (SOURCE / name).open(encoding=\\\"utf-8-sig\\\", newline=\\\"\\\") as stream:\\n\",\"        return list(csv.DictReader(stream))\\n\",\"\\n\",\"\\n\",\"def write(output_dir, name, fields, rows):\\n\",\"    output_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n\",\"    with (output_dir / name).open(\\\"w\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\", newline=\\\"\\\") as stream:\\n\",\"        writer = csv.DictWriter(stream, fieldnames=fields)\\n\",\"        writer.writeheader()\\n\",\"        writer.writerows(rows)\\n\",\"\\n\",\"items = read(\\\"controlled_items.csv\\\")\\n\",\"absent = read(\\\"no_match_queries.csv\\\")\\n\",\"if len({item[\\\"item_group_id\\\"] for item in items}) != len(items):\\n\",\"    raise ValueError(\\\"Controlled item groups must be unique\\\")\\n\",\"inventory = read(\\\"../../raw/campus/office_inventory_aggregate.csv\\\")\\n\",\"quantities = Counter()\\n\",\"for row in inventory:\\n\",\"    quantities[row[\\\"period\\\"]] += int(row[\\\"quantity\\\"])\\n\",\"if dict(quantities) != {\\\"2026-06_07\\\": 388, \\\"2026-08\\\": 299}:\\n\",\"    raise ValueError(f\\\"Aggregate transcription does not reconcile: {dict(quantities)}\\\")\\n\",\"found = []\\n\",\"lost = []\\n\",\"labels = []\\n\",\"queries = []\\n\",\"for item in items:\\n\",\"    group = item[\\\"item_group_id\\\"]\\n\",\"    found.append(dict(found_id=f\\\"f-{group}\\\", item_group_id=group, category=item[\\\"category\\\"],\\n\",\"                      description=item[\\\"found_description\\\"], colour=item[\\\"colour\\\"], brand=item[\\\"brand\\\"],\\n\",\"                      distinguishing_attributes=\\\"\\\", location=item[\\\"location\\\"], event_date=\\\"\\\",\\n\",\"                      report_status=\\\"active\\\", source_type=item[\\\"source_type\\\"], split=item[\\\"split\\\"]))\\n\",\"    lost.append(dict(lost_id=f\\\"l-{group}\\\", item_group_id=group, category=item[\\\"category\\\"],\\n\",\"                     description=item[\\\"lost_description\\\"], colour=item[\\\"colour\\\"], brand=item[\\\"brand\\\"],\\n\",\"                     last_seen_location=item[\\\"location\\\"], date_lost=\\\"\\\", source_type=item[\\\"source_type\\\"],\\n\",\"                     split=item[\\\"split\\\"]))\\n\",\"for item in items:\\n\",\"    group, split = item[\\\"item_group_id\\\"], item[\\\"split\\\"]\\n\",\"    lost_id = f\\\"l-{group}\\\"\\n\",\"    for candidate in items:\\n\",\"        if candidate[\\\"split\\\"] != split:\\n\",\"            continue\\n\",\"        same = candidate[\\\"item_group_id\\\"] == group\\n\",\"        labels.append(dict(lost_id=lost_id, found_id=f\\\"f-{candidate['item_group_id']}\\\",\\n\",\"                           label=int(same), label_source=\\\"controlled_fictional_identity\\\",\\n\",\"                           item_group_id=group, reviewer=\\\"pending_independent_review\\\", split=split))\\n\",\"    queries.append(dict(query_id=f\\\"q-{group}\\\", lost_id=lost_id, relevant_found_ids=f\\\"f-{group}\\\",\\n\",\"                        candidate_pool_id=\\\"all_constructed_found_v1\\\", has_match=1, split=split))\\n\",\"for row in absent:\\n\",\"    lost.append(dict(lost_id=row[\\\"lost_id\\\"], item_group_id=row[\\\"lost_id\\\"], category=row[\\\"category\\\"],\\n\",\"                     description=row[\\\"description\\\"], colour=row[\\\"colour\\\"], brand=row[\\\"brand\\\"],\\n\",\"                     last_seen_location=row[\\\"location\\\"], date_lost=\\\"\\\", source_type=row[\\\"source_type\\\"],\\n\",\"                     split=row[\\\"split\\\"]))\\n\",\"    queries.append(dict(query_id=f\\\"q-{row['lost_id']}\\\", lost_id=row[\\\"lost_id\\\"], relevant_found_ids=\\\"\\\",\\n\",\"                        candidate_pool_id=\\\"all_constructed_found_v1\\\", has_match=0, split=row[\\\"split\\\"]))\\n\",\"\\n\",\"write(output_dir, \\\"found_reports.csv\\\", list(found[0]), found)\\n\",\"write(output_dir, \\\"lost_reports.csv\\\", list(lost[0]), lost)\\n\",\"write(output_dir, \\\"match_labels.csv\\\", list(labels[0]), labels)\\n\",\"write(output_dir, \\\"evaluation_queries.csv\\\", list(queries[0]), queries)\\n\",\"(output_dir / \\\"candidate_pools.json\\\").write_text(json.dumps({\\\"all_constructed_found_v1\\\": [r[\\\"found_id\\\"] for r in found]}, indent=2) + \\\"\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n\",\"audit = {\\\"inventory_quantities\\\": dict(quantities), \\\"found_records\\\": len(found),\\n\",\"         \\\"lost_reports\\\": len(lost), \\\"controlled_positive_labels\\\": len(items),\\n\",\"         \\\"controlled_negative_labels\\\": len(labels) - len(items), \\\"no_match_queries\\\": len(absent),\\n\",\"         \\\"candidate_pool_size\\\": len(found), \\\"source_type\\\": \\\"AI-authored fictional controlled examples\\\",\\n\",\"         \\\"review\\\": \\\"Independent student review pending; no genuine same-item labels or campus performance.\\\"}\\n\",\"(output_dir / \\\"provenance.json\\\").write_text(json.dumps(audit, indent=2) + \\\"\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n\",\"print(\\\"Prepared:\\\", len(found), \\\"found,\\\", len(lost), \\\"lost,\\\", len(labels), \\\"pairs\\\")\"],\"execution_count\":null,\"outputs\":[]},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"id\":\"quality\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"### 2.1 Data quality and exploratory analysis\\n\",\"Check mandatory fields, duplicate IDs, label validity, positive/negative identity consistency, candidate references and split boundaries. The full reusable validator runs in addition to the visible checks below. A successful structural check does not certify real-world label truth.\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"id\":\"validation-audit\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"from scripts.validate_ranking_dataset import validate\\n\",\"# Reload written CSVs so labels and split types exactly match the evaluator.\\n\",\"def read_csv(name):\\n\",\"    return pd.read_csv(DATA / name, dtype=str, keep_default_na=False).to_dict(\\\"records\\\")\\n\",\"\\n\",\"found = read_csv(\\\"found_reports.csv\\\")\\n\",\"lost = read_csv(\\\"lost_reports.csv\\\")\\n\",\"labels = read_csv(\\\"match_labels.csv\\\")\\n\",\"queries = read_csv(\\\"evaluation_queries.csv\\\")\\n\",\"for rows, key in [(found, \\\"found_id\\\"), (lost, \\\"lost_id\\\")]:\\n\",\"    ids = [row[key] for row in rows]\\n\",\"    assert len(ids) == len(set(ids)) and all(ids)\\n\",\"    assert all(row[\\\"description\\\"].strip() for row in rows)\\n\",\"assert {r[\\\"label\\\"] for r in labels} == {\\\"0\\\", \\\"1\\\"}\\n\",\"group_split = defaultdict(set)\\n\",\"for row in found + lost:\\n\",\"    group_split[row[\\\"item_group_id\\\"]].add(row[\\\"split\\\"])\\n\",\"assert all(len(splits) == 1 for splits in group_split.values())\\n\",\"validation_audit = validate(DATA)\\n\",\"assert validation_audit[\\\"valid\\\"], validation_audit[\\\"errors\\\"]\\n\",\"print(\\\"Structural validation passed:\\\", validation_audit[\\\"counts\\\"])\\n\",\"print(\\\"Label counts:\\\", validation_audit[\\\"label_counts\\\"])\\n\",\"display(pd.DataFrame(found)[[\\\"found_id\\\", \\\"category\\\", \\\"description\\\", \\\"split\\\"]].head(4))\\n\",\"display(pd.crosstab(pd.DataFrame(queries)[\\\"split\\\"], pd.DataFrame(queries)[\\\"has_match\\\"])\\n\",\"        .rename(columns={\\\"0\\\":\\\"no match\\\", \\\"1\\\":\\\"matched\\\"}).reindex([\\\"train\\\",\\\"validation\\\",\\\"test\\\"], fill_value=0))\"],\"execution_count\":null,\"outputs\":[]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"id\":\"data-eda\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"from statistics import median\\n\",\"for name, rows in [(\\\"found\\\", found), (\\\"lost\\\", lost)]:\\n\",\"    lengths = [len(row[\\\"description\\\"]) for row in rows]\\n\",\"    print(name, \\\"description length min/median/max:\\\", min(lengths), median(lengths), max(lengths))\\n\",\"split_counts = pd.Series({s: sum(q[\\\"split\\\"] == s for q in queries) for s in [\\\"train\\\",\\\"validation\\\",\\\"test\\\"]})\\n\",\"ax = split_counts.plot(kind=\\\"bar\\\", figsize=(5.5,3), rot=0, title=\\\"Queries per split\\\")\\n\",\"ax.set_ylabel(\\\"Queries\\\")\\n\",\"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\"plt.show()\\n\",\"display(pd.DataFrame(labels).groupby([\\\"split\\\",\\\"label\\\"]).size().unstack(fill_value=0))\"],\"execution_count\":null,\"outputs\":[]},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"id\":\"base-model\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"## 3. Modelling: Logistic Regression base model\\n\",\"The earlier supervised approach estimates a same-item pair score from 14 engineered features. A supervised model learns from examples with known labels. Logistic Regression applies a sigmoid to a weighted sum of features; here its score is used to rank pairs, not as a verified ownership probability.\\n\",\"\\n\",\"Features capture shared description words (Jaccard similarity = shared words / unique words), category/colour/brand/model/material agreement or disagreement, distinctive features, location and bounded time difference. Missing values do not become conflicts; missing timestamps use the existing 48-hour default. Balanced class weights reduce the dominance of the negative class. See the separate historical base notebook for its earlier experiment; this section refits on the current controlled benchmark.\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"id\":\"baseline-features\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"from matching_system.logistic_regression_features import FEATURE_NAMES, pair_features\\n\",\"from matching_system.models import Report\\n\",\"from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\\n\",\"from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import TfidfVectorizer\\n\",\"from sklearn.metrics.pairwise import cosine_similarity\\n\",\"\\n\",\"def tokens(value):\\n\",\"    from matching_system.nlp_retrieval import normalize_report_text\\n\",\"    return set(normalize_report_text(value).split())\\n\",\"\\n\",\"\\n\",\"def keyword(lost, found):\\n\",\"    left, right = tokens(lost[\\\"description\\\"]), tokens(found[\\\"description\\\"])\\n\",\"    return len(left & right) / len(left | right) if left and right else 0.0\\n\",\"\\n\",\"\\n\",\"def attributes(lost, found):\\n\",\"    score = 0.0\\n\",\"    for field, weight in ((\\\"category\\\", 0.5), (\\\"colour\\\", 0.25), (\\\"brand\\\", 0.25)):\\n\",\"        a, b = lost.get(field, \\\"\\\").casefold(), found.get(field, \\\"\\\").casefold()\\n\",\"        if a and b:\\n\",\"            score += weight if a == b else -weight\\n\",\"    return max(0.0, score)\\n\",\"\\n\",\"\\n\",\"def as_report(row, kind):\\n\",\"    return Report(report_id=row[f\\\"{kind}_id\\\"], report_type=kind, description=row[\\\"description\\\"],\\n\",\"                  category=row[\\\"category\\\"], colour=row.get(\\\"colour\\\", \\\"\\\"), brand=row.get(\\\"brand\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n\",\"                  location=row.get(\\\"last_seen_location\\\" if kind == \\\"lost\\\" else \\\"location\\\", \\\"\\\"))\\n\",\"\\n\",\"found = {row[\\\"found_id\\\"]: row for row in found}\\n\",\"lost = {row[\\\"lost_id\\\"]: row for row in lost}\\n\",\"pools = json.loads((DATA / \\\"candidate_pools.json\\\").read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\"))\\n\",\"assert len(pools) == 1\\n\",\"found_ids = next(iter(pools.values()))\\n\",\"feature_cache = {}\\n\",\"for q in queries:\\n\",\"    for fid in found_ids:\\n\",\"        key = (q[\\\"lost_id\\\"], fid)\\n\",\"        feature_cache[key] = pair_features(as_report(lost[key[0]], \\\"lost\\\"), as_report(found[fid], \\\"found\\\"))\\n\",\"training = [r for r in labels if r[\\\"split\\\"] == \\\"train\\\" and r[\\\"label\\\"] in {\\\"0\\\",\\\"1\\\"}]\\n\",\"x_train = np.array([[feature_cache[(r[\\\"lost_id\\\"], r[\\\"found_id\\\"])][name] for name in FEATURE_NAMES] for r in training])\\n\",\"y_train = np.array([int(r[\\\"label\\\"]) for r in training])\\n\",\"print(\\\"Training matrix:\\\", x_train.shape, \\\"| positive labels:\\\", int(y_train.sum()))\\n\",\"display(pd.DataFrame(x_train[:3], columns=FEATURE_NAMES).T.rename(columns={0:\\\"pair 1\\\",1:\\\"pair 2\\\",2:\\\"pair 3\\\"}))\"],\"execution_count\":null,\"outputs\":[]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"id\":\"baseline-fit\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"classifier = LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000, class_weight=\\\"balanced\\\", random_state=42)\\n\",\"classifier.fit(x_train, y_train)\\n\",\"all_keys = list(feature_cache)\\n\",\"x_all = np.array([[feature_cache[key][name] for name in FEATURE_NAMES] for key in all_keys])\\n\",\"classifier_scores = dict(zip(all_keys, classifier.predict_proba(x_all)[:,1]))\\n\",\"print(\\\"Model fitted. Feature count:\\\", len(FEATURE_NAMES))\\n\",\"display(pd.DataFrame({\\\"feature\\\": FEATURE_NAMES, \\\"coefficient\\\": classifier.coef_[0]}).round(3))\"],\"execution_count\":null,\"outputs\":[]},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"id\":\"nlp-method\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"## 4. Modelling: Natural Language Processing with TF-IDF\\n\",\"Natural Language Processing (NLP) converts written descriptions into comparable numeric representations. Normalization lowercases text, removes punctuation and collapses whitespace; e.g. \\\"BLACK HP Laptop-Charger!\\\" becomes \\\"black hp laptop charger\\\". Unigrams are single words and bigrams are two-word phrases.\\n\",\"\\n\",\"**TF-IDF (term frequency–inverse document frequency)** weights a term by its frequency in the description and how uncommon it is across the fitted corpus. Scikit-learn uses smoothed IDF: idf(t) = ln((1 + N)/(1 + df(t))) + 1, where N is the number of documents and df(t) is the number containing t. It then L2-normalizes the vectors.\\n\",\"**Cosine similarity** compares vectors using their dot product divided by their lengths. A value of 1 means identical vector direction; 0 means no shared weighted terms. It measures lexical similarity, not physical identity.\\n\",\"\\n\",\"The offline experiment fits on training descriptions, with scikit-learn's lowercasing/tokenization, accent stripping and word n-grams. The actual worker explicitly normalizes item names and descriptions and indexes the current found inventory; section 7A evaluates that exact path separately.\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"id\":\"tfidf-fit\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"from matching_system.nlp_retrieval import normalize_report_text\\n\",\"train_found = [r for r in found.values() if r[\\\"split\\\"] == \\\"train\\\"]\\n\",\"train_lost = [r for r in lost.values() if r[\\\"split\\\"] == \\\"train\\\"]\\n\",\"vectorizer = TfidfVectorizer(ngram_range=(1, 2), strip_accents=\\\"unicode\\\")\\n\",\"vectorizer.fit([r[\\\"description\\\"] for r in train_found + train_lost])\\n\",\"found_matrix = vectorizer.transform([found[fid][\\\"description\\\"] for fid in found_ids])\\n\",\"lost_matrix = vectorizer.transform([lost[q[\\\"lost_id\\\"]][\\\"description\\\"] for q in queries])\\n\",\"cosine = cosine_similarity(lost_matrix, found_matrix)\\n\",\"print(\\\"Normalization:\\\", normalize_report_text(\\\"BLACK HP Laptop-Charger!\\\"))\\n\",\"print(\\\"Training documents:\\\", len(train_found) + len(train_lost), \\\"| vocabulary:\\\", len(vectorizer.vocabulary_))\\n\",\"print(\\\"Found vector shape:\\\", found_matrix.shape, \\\"| similarity matrix:\\\", cosine.shape)\\n\",\"display(pd.DataFrame(cosine[:3,:5], index=[q[\\\"lost_id\\\"] for q in queries[:3]], columns=found_ids[:5]).round(3))\"],\"execution_count\":null,\"outputs\":[]},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"id\":\"validation\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"## 5. Validation and model selection\\n\",\"Compare five methods on the same fixed inventory. Keyword overlap is a simple word-set baseline; structured attributes use category (0.50), colour (0.25) and brand (0.25), subtracting the weight for explicit conflicts. Logistic Regression uses the fitted classifier; TF-IDF uses cosine; hybrid combines TF-IDF and structured scores.\\n\",\"\\n\",\"Top-1 = fraction of matched queries whose correct record ranks first. Recall@5 = fraction of relevant records retrieved in the first five (one correct item per matched query here). MRR (mean reciprocal rank) averages 1/rank of the first correct record. For no-match cases, count queries whose top score exceeds a validation-selected experimental cutoff. Choose hybrid weight by validation Recall@5, then MRR, then smaller TF-IDF weight. No settings are selected on the test queries.\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"id\":\"ranking-metrics\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"def ranking_metrics(queries, scores, found_ids):\\n\",\"    matched, unmatched = [], []\\n\",\"    for query in queries:\\n\",\"        ranked = sorted(found_ids, key=lambda fid: (-scores[(query[\\\"lost_id\\\"], fid)], fid))\\n\",\"        relevant = set(filter(None, query[\\\"relevant_found_ids\\\"].split(\\\"|\\\")))\\n\",\"        top = scores[(query[\\\"lost_id\\\"], ranked[0])] if ranked else 0.0\\n\",\"        if relevant:\\n\",\"            positions = [i + 1 for i, fid in enumerate(ranked) if fid in relevant]\\n\",\"            matched.append({\\\"query_id\\\": query[\\\"query_id\\\"], \\\"first_rank\\\": min(positions) if positions else None,\\n\",\"                            \\\"recall_at_5\\\": len([p for p in positions if p <= 5]) / len(relevant)})\\n\",\"        else:\\n\",\"            unmatched.append({\\\"query_id\\\": query[\\\"query_id\\\"], \\\"top_score\\\": top})\\n\",\"    n = len(matched)\\n\",\"    return {\\\"matched_queries\\\": n, \\\"no_match_queries\\\": len(unmatched), \\\"candidate_pool_size\\\": len(found_ids),\\n\",\"            \\\"top1_accuracy\\\": sum(row[\\\"first_rank\\\"] == 1 for row in matched) / n if n else None,\\n\",\"            \\\"recall_at_5\\\": sum(row[\\\"recall_at_5\\\"] for row in matched) / n if n else None,\\n\",\"            \\\"mrr\\\": sum(1 / row[\\\"first_rank\\\"] if row[\\\"first_rank\\\"] else 0 for row in matched) / n if n else None,\\n\",\"            \\\"matched_details\\\": matched, \\\"no_match_details\\\": unmatched}\\n\",\"\\n\",\"scores = {name: {} for name in (\\\"keyword\\\", \\\"attributes\\\", \\\"logistic_regression\\\", \\\"tfidf\\\", \\\"hybrid\\\")}\\n\",\"for qi, q in enumerate(queries):\\n\",\"    for fi, fid in enumerate(found_ids):\\n\",\"        key = (q[\\\"lost_id\\\"], fid)\\n\",\"        scores[\\\"keyword\\\"][key] = keyword(lost[key[0]], found[fid])\\n\",\"        scores[\\\"attributes\\\"][key] = attributes(lost[key[0]], found[fid])\\n\",\"        scores[\\\"logistic_regression\\\"][key] = float(classifier_scores[key])\\n\",\"        scores[\\\"tfidf\\\"][key] = float(cosine[qi, fi])\\n\",\"validation = [q for q in queries if q[\\\"split\\\"] == \\\"validation\\\"]\\n\",\"choices = []\\n\",\"for weight in (0.25, 0.5, 0.75):\\n\",\"    candidate = {key: weight * scores[\\\"tfidf\\\"][key] + (1 - weight) * scores[\\\"attributes\\\"][key] for key in all_keys}\\n\",\"    metric = ranking_metrics(validation, candidate, found_ids)\\n\",\"    choices.append((metric[\\\"recall_at_5\\\"], metric[\\\"mrr\\\"], weight, candidate))\\n\",\"_, _, weight, scores[\\\"hybrid\\\"] = max(choices, key=lambda item: (item[0], item[1], -item[2]))\\n\",\"display(pd.DataFrame([{\\\"TF-IDF weight\\\": w, \\\"Validation Recall@5\\\": recall, \\\"Validation MRR\\\": mrr}\\n\",\"                       for recall, mrr, w, _ in choices]).round(3))\\n\",\"print(\\\"Selected hybrid TF-IDF weight:\\\", weight)\"],\"execution_count\":null,\"outputs\":[]},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"id\":\"evaluation\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"## 6. Held-out evaluation\\n\",\"Use the ten test queries only after tuning. Eight have a designated match; two have none. For the offline experiment, the ranking includes all 24 candidates, even zero scores. The no-match cutoff comes from the single validation no-match query. It is not a calibrated confidence threshold and is not applied by the operational worker.\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"id\":\"test-results\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"output = {\\\"provenance\\\": \\\"AI-authored controlled fiction; no real-campus accuracy claim\\\",\\n\",\"          \\\"dataset\\\": validation_audit[\\\"counts\\\"], \\\"sklearn_version\\\": sklearn.__version__,\\n\",\"          \\\"tfidf\\\": {\\\"fit_split\\\": \\\"train\\\", \\\"ngram_range\\\": [1, 2], \\\"vocabulary_size\\\": len(vectorizer.vocabulary_)},\\n\",\"          \\\"logistic_regression\\\": {\\\"fit_split\\\": \\\"train\\\", \\\"pair_count\\\": len(training), \\\"features\\\": list(FEATURE_NAMES)},\\n\",\"          \\\"hybrid\\\": {\\\"tfidf_weight_selected_on_validation\\\": weight}, \\\"methods\\\": {}}\\n\",\"for name, method_scores in scores.items():\\n\",\"    val = ranking_metrics(validation, method_scores, found_ids)\\n\",\"    no_match_top = [row[\\\"top_score\\\"] for row in val[\\\"no_match_details\\\"]]\\n\",\"    threshold = max(no_match_top, default=0.0) + 1e-9\\n\",\"    test = ranking_metrics([q for q in queries if q[\\\"split\\\"] == \\\"test\\\"], method_scores, found_ids)\\n\",\"    false_suggestions = sum(row[\\\"top_score\\\"] >= threshold for row in test[\\\"no_match_details\\\"])\\n\",\"    output[\\\"methods\\\"][name] = {\\\"validation\\\": val, \\\"test\\\": test,\\n\",\"                                \\\"strong_match_threshold_from_validation\\\": threshold,\\n\",\"                                \\\"test_no_match_false_suggestions\\\": false_suggestions,\\n\",\"                                \\\"test_no_match_denominator\\\": test[\\\"no_match_queries\\\"]}\\n\",\"results = output\\n\",\"summary = pd.DataFrame([\\n\",\"    {\\\"Method\\\": name, \\\"Top-1\\\": info[\\\"test\\\"][\\\"top1_accuracy\\\"],\\n\",\"     \\\"Recall@5\\\": info[\\\"test\\\"][\\\"recall_at_5\\\"], \\\"MRR\\\": info[\\\"test\\\"][\\\"mrr\\\"],\\n\",\"     \\\"False suggestions\\\": f\\\"{info['test_no_match_false_suggestions']}/{info['test_no_match_denominator']}\\\"}\\n\",\"    for name, info in results[\\\"methods\\\"].items()\\n\",\"]).set_index(\\\"Method\\\")\\n\",\"display(summary.round(3))\\n\",\"(RUN_DIR / \\\"ranking_benchmark.json\\\").write_text(json.dumps(results, indent=2), encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n\",\"# Check the visible notebook implementation against the maintained evaluator.\\n\",\"from scripts.evaluate_ranking_benchmark import main as maintained_evaluator\\n\",\"import contextlib, io\\n\",\"with contextlib.redirect_stdout(io.StringIO()):\\n\",\"    reference = maintained_evaluator(DATA, RUN_DIR / \\\"reference_results.json\\\")\\n\",\"for name in results[\\\"methods\\\"]:\\n\",\"    for metric in [\\\"top1_accuracy\\\", \\\"recall_at_5\\\", \\\"mrr\\\"]:\\n\",\"        assert np.isclose(results[\\\"methods\\\"][name][\\\"test\\\"][metric],\\n\",\"                          reference[\\\"methods\\\"][name][\\\"test\\\"][metric]), (name, metric)\\n\",\"    assert results[\\\"methods\\\"][name][\\\"test_no_match_false_suggestions\\\"] == reference[\\\"methods\\\"][name][\\\"test_no_match_false_suggestions\\\"]\\n\",\"print(\\\"Visible notebook comparison agrees with the maintained evaluator.\\\")\"],\"execution_count\":null,\"outputs\":[]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"id\":\"test-chart\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"ax = summary[[\\\"Top-1\\\",\\\"Recall@5\\\",\\\"MRR\\\"]].plot(kind=\\\"bar\\\", figsize=(9,4), rot=15)\\n\",\"ax.set(title=\\\"Offline benchmark — eight matched test queries\\\", ylabel=\\\"Fraction\\\", ylim=(0,1.08))\\n\",\"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\"plt.show()\"],\"execution_count\":null,\"outputs\":[]},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"id\":\"explanation\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"## 7. Explainability and operational matching logic\\n\",\"The operational ranker is the lightweight TF-IDF prototype. It fits a vectorizer on current found item names and descriptions; a lost query is transformed using the same vocabulary. Return up to five positive-scoring items, sorted by descending similarity, breaking ties by ID. Separate knowledge rules assess category, location and event-date facts after retrieval. They guide staff review, not the ordering. No CLIP, image model, probability claim or automatic handover.\\n\",\"\\n\",\"The following cell exposes the numerical steps and calls the same knowledge functions as the operational implementation. The assertion checks candidate order against the actual TfidfMatcher, rather than assuming the illustrated implementation matches.\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"id\":\"operational-example\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"from matching_system.nlp_retrieval import TextReport\\n\",\"from matching_system.matching_agent import assess_candidate\\n\",\"from matching_system.staff_workflow_agent import recommend_staff_workflow\\n\",\"from matching_system.pipeline import explain_candidate\\n\",\"from service.inference import TfidfMatcher\\n\",\"\\n\",\"def runtime_row(row, kind):\\n\",\"    return {\\\"id\\\": row[f\\\"{kind}_id\\\"], \\\"report_type\\\": kind,\\n\",\"            \\\"description\\\": row[\\\"description\\\"], \\\"item_name\\\": row.get(\\\"item_name\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n\",\"            \\\"category_id\\\": row.get(\\\"category\\\") or None,\\n\",\"            \\\"location_id\\\": row.get(\\\"last_seen_location\\\" if kind == \\\"lost\\\" else \\\"location\\\") or None,\\n\",\"            \\\"event_date\\\": row.get(\\\"date_lost\\\" if kind == \\\"lost\\\" else \\\"event_date\\\") or None}\\n\",\"\\n\",\"def to_text_report(row):\\n\",\"    return TextReport(row[\\\"id\\\"], row[\\\"report_type\\\"], row[\\\"description\\\"],\\n\",\"                      item_name=row.get(\\\"item_name\\\", \\\"\\\"), category_id=row.get(\\\"category_id\\\"),\\n\",\"                      location_id=row.get(\\\"location_id\\\"), event_date=row.get(\\\"event_date\\\"))\\n\",\"\\n\",\"inventory_rows = [runtime_row(found[fid], \\\"found\\\") for fid in found_ids]\\n\",\"query_row = runtime_row(lost[\\\"l-g017\\\"], \\\"lost\\\")\\n\",\"corpus = [normalize_report_text(f\\\"{row['item_name']} {row['description']}\\\") for row in inventory_rows]\\n\",\"query_text = normalize_report_text(f\\\"{query_row['item_name']} {query_row['description']}\\\")\\n\",\"live_vectorizer = TfidfVectorizer(ngram_range=(1,2), strip_accents=\\\"unicode\\\")\\n\",\"inventory_matrix = live_vectorizer.fit_transform(corpus)\\n\",\"query_vector = live_vectorizer.transform([query_text])\\n\",\"similarities = cosine_similarity(query_vector, inventory_matrix)[0]\\n\",\"ordered = sorted([(row, float(score)) for row, score in zip(inventory_rows, similarities) if score > 0],\\n\",\"                 key=lambda pair: (-pair[1], pair[0][\\\"id\\\"]))[:5]\\n\",\"actual = TfidfMatcher().recommend(query_row, inventory_rows)\\n\",\"assert [row[\\\"id\\\"] for row, _ in ordered] == [r[\\\"found_report_id\\\"] for r in actual]\\n\",\"for row, score in ordered:\\n\",\"    assessment = assess_candidate(to_text_report(query_row), to_text_report(row), round(score, 6))\\n\",\"    workflow = recommend_staff_workflow(assessment)\\n\",\"    print(row[\\\"id\\\"], \\\"score:\\\", round(score, 6), \\\"|\\\", explain_candidate(assessment, workflow))\\n\",\"if actual:\\n\",\"    display(pd.DataFrame(actual[0][\\\"facts\\\"]))\\n\",\"print(\\\"Operational candidate order verified against the deployed-code ranker (in process).\\\")\"],\"execution_count\":null,\"outputs\":[]},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"id\":\"runtime-eval\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"### 7A. Operational matching pipeline evaluation\\n\",\"The current app worker calls TfidfMatcher. Evaluate it separately on the same ten held-out queries and frozen 24-record inventory, without using the offline cutoff. The benchmark lacks separate item names, so leave them blank. MRR@5 assigns zero if the correct item is not among the five returned records. A no-match false suggestion here means any result under the operational positive-score policy. These measures concern retrieval for new lost reports, not end-to-end Firestore or mobile connectivity.\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"id\":\"runtime-metrics\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"pool = pools\\n\",\"matcher = TfidfMatcher()\\n\",\"details = []\\n\",\"for q in queries:\\n\",\"    if q['split'] != 'test':\\n\",\"        continue\\n\",\"    inventory_rows = [runtime_row(found[fid], 'found') for fid in pool[q['candidate_pool_id']]]\\n\",\"    ranked = matcher.recommend(runtime_row(lost[q['lost_id']], 'lost'), inventory_rows)\\n\",\"    ids = [m['found_report_id'] for m in ranked]\\n\",\"    relevant = set(filter(None, q['relevant_found_ids'].split('|')))\\n\",\"    positions = [i + 1 for i, fid in enumerate(ids) if fid in relevant]\\n\",\"    details.append({'query': q['query_id'], 'has_match': bool(relevant),\\n\",\"                    'first_rank': min(positions) if positions else None,\\n\",\"                    'recall5': len(positions)/len(relevant) if relevant else None,\\n\",\"                    'candidate_count': len(ids),\\n\",\"                    'top_score': ranked[0]['text_similarity'] if ranked else None,\\n\",\"                    'top_candidate': ids[0] if ids else None,\\n\",\"                    'explanation': ranked[0]['explanation'] if ranked else 'No lexical candidates'})\\n\",\"matched = [d for d in details if d['has_match']]\\n\",\"unmatched = [d for d in details if not d['has_match']]\\n\",\"assert len(matched) == 8 and len(unmatched) == 2\\n\",\"print('Operational model:', matcher.version)\\n\",\"print('Top-1:', sum(d['first_rank'] == 1 for d in matched)/len(matched))\\n\",\"print('Recall@5:', sum(d['recall5'] for d in matched)/len(matched))\\n\",\"print('MRR@5:', sum(1/d['first_rank'] if d['first_rank'] else 0 for d in matched)/len(matched))\\n\",\"print('No-match queries with suggestions:', sum(d['candidate_count'] > 0 for d in unmatched), '/', len(unmatched))\\n\",\"display(pd.DataFrame(details).drop(columns='explanation'))\\n\",\"print('Example explanation:', details[0]['explanation'])\"],\"execution_count\":null,\"outputs\":[]},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"id\":\"deployment\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"## 8. Integration and input validation\\n\",\"The local preview exercises the same NLP and explanation pipeline but does not persist reports or authenticate users. Test a valid report and invalid descriptions/dates. The optional HTTP check runs the preview on port 8001; the actual Android service is service.api:app on port 8000, with Firebase emulators and the separate worker. The local mode is the presentation deployment; no paid hosting is required.\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"id\":\"preview\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"from pydantic import ValidationError\\n\",\"from matching_system.api import PreviewRequest, preview_matches\\n\",\"request = PreviewRequest(item_name='Metal water bottle',description='Blue bottle with a scratched lid',category_id='metal_water_bottle',location_id='msb',event_date='2026-11-10',limit=3)\\n\",\"body = preview_matches(request)\\n\",\"print('status:', body['status'], 'first ID:', body['matches'][0]['found_report_id'])\\n\",\"print('explanation:', body['matches'][0]['explanation'])\\n\",\"for label, values in [('blank description', {'item_name':'Water bottle','description':''}), ('invalid calendar date', {'item_name':'Water bottle','description':'Blue bottle','event_date':'2026-02-30'})]:\\n\",\"    try:\\n\",\"        PreviewRequest(**values)\\n\",\"    except ValidationError:\\n\",\"        print(label + ': rejected')\"],\"execution_count\":null,\"outputs\":[]},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"id\":\"http-preview\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"### 8A. Optional HTTP preview and required application demonstration\\n\",\"To run the optional preview check, start `python -m uvicorn matching_system.api:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8001` and set NLP_LIVE_HTTP_DEMO=1 before starting the notebook kernel. This check is optional and does not prove Android integration.\\n\",\"For the actual demo use the local presentation startup instructions in docs/LOCAL_PRESENTATION.md (PR #18 until merged). Run the authenticated API, emulator and worker; use the student and office accounts, two valid descriptions, an invalid input and actual ranked results with explanations. All three presenters attend with cameras on. Do not report device success without observing it.\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"id\":\"http-check\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"import os\\n\",\"import json\\n\",\"from urllib.error import HTTPError, URLError\\n\",\"from urllib.request import Request, urlopen\\n\",\"\\n\",\"def post_preview(payload):\\n\",\"    req = Request('http://127.0.0.1:8001/preview/matches', data=json.dumps(payload).encode('utf-8'), headers={'Content-Type':'application/json'}, method='POST')\\n\",\"    try:\\n\",\"        with urlopen(req, timeout=5) as response:\\n\",\"            return response.status, json.loads(response.read().decode('utf-8'))\\n\",\"    except HTTPError as error:\\n\",\"        return error.code, json.loads(error.read().decode('utf-8'))\\n\",\"\\n\",\"if os.environ.get('NLP_LIVE_HTTP_DEMO') == '1':\\n\",\"    valid = {'item_name':'Metal water bottle','description':'Blue bottle with a scratched lid','category_id':'metal_water_bottle','location_id':'msb','event_date':'2026-11-10','limit':3}\\n\",\"    status, result = post_preview(valid)\\n\",\"    print('valid request:', status, result['status'], 'candidate count:', len(result['matches']))\\n\",\"    print('first explanation:', result['matches'][0]['explanation'] if result['matches'] else 'No candidate in the demo inventory')\\n\",\"    print('blank description:', post_preview({**valid, 'description':''})[0])\\n\",\"    print('invalid date:', post_preview({**valid, 'event_date':'2026-02-30'})[0])\\n\",\"else:\\n\",\"    print('Live HTTP check skipped. Start the local API and set NLP_LIVE_HTTP_DEMO=1 to run it.')\"],\"execution_count\":null,\"outputs\":[]},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"id\":\"limits\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"## 9. Interpretation and next steps\\n\",\"Compare results after execution. The previous committed controlled experiment reported offline TF-IDF Top-1 2/8, Recall@5 4/8, and two false suggestions among two no-match queries; attributes, Logistic Regression and hybrid ranked all eight designated matches first. Reused structured fields in the authored fixtures inflate apparent performance. The active TF-IDF ranker remains a lightweight operational prototype, not the winner of the offline comparison. Lexical similarity can miss synonyms and paraphrases or suggest unrelated items that share words. A missing candidate does not prove absence.\\n\",\"\\n\",\"**Next steps:** independently verify the office transcription and benchmark labels; collect permitted genuine item-level pairs and a larger independent test set; test paraphrases and rejection; verify device-level reporting and job completion. Keep staff review and privacy protections. The model is a candidate ranking aid, not proof of ownership.\\n\",\"\\n\",\"**Submission checklist:** the base notebook is retained; this notebook includes the data mining stages and actual model logic; run all cells and save genuine outputs, review the numbers, rehearse the app and comply with instructor AI-use requirements.\"]}],\"metadata\":{\"kernelspec\":{\"display_name\":\"Python 3.12\",\"language\":\"python\",\"name\":\"python3\"},\"language_info\":{\"name\":\"python\",\"version\":\"3.12\"}},\"nbformat\":4,\"nbformat_minor\":5}")
